1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. Mongolians saw — seven old men.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In Mongolian it is Doloon Övgön: the
Seven Old Men.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
More often, Doloon Burkhan: the Seven
Buddhas. Some still sprinkle a little
milk in offering, morning and evening.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Eight orphan brothers saved a queen from
a monster.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The king threw a golden arrow into the
sky. The youngest caught it.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
He became the Pole Star. His seven
brothers, the Dipper, visit him nightly.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
A gadas is a wooden post driven into the
steppe to tether animals.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The Dipper rides high in the northeast.
Extend the bowl’s two outer stars over
five times to the stake.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The seven brothers circle the stake all
night, like horses tied to a post.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
In Ulaanbaatar, the stake stands 48°
high. The Dipper never sets: all seven
brothers, every night.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
In a world on the move, they tied the
whole sky to one fixed stake.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Arc to Arcturus: spring star-hopping.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

